---
import '@fontsource-variable/inter';
import '@fontsource-variable/manrope';
import '../styles/global.css';
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover" />
  <title>Privacy | HDFC Bank Student Project</title>
</head>
<body>
  <main class="wrap privacy-wrap" style="max-width:800px; line-height:1.7">
    <a class="back-link" href="/">Back to home</a>
    <h1 style="font-size:2rem; margin-block:20px">Privacy notice</h1>
    <p>This independent student project uses fictional accounts and virtual funds.</p>
    <h2 style="font-size:1.2rem; margin-block:18px 6px">Information stored</h2>
    <p>We store your name, email address, optional phone number and address, account details and transaction history to operate your account. We also store saved recipients, nominee and guardian details you provide, demo card numbers, security codes, networks and freeze status, preferences and support requests. Passwords, transaction PINs and short-lived recovery codes are stored as hashes. Google sign-in uses your verified Google identity.</p>
    <h2 style="font-size:1.2rem; margin-block:18px 6px">Service providers</h2>
    <p>Render hosts the application, Aiven hosts the database, and Google provides optional sign-in. These providers process information needed to deliver their services.</p>
    <h2 style="font-size:1.2rem; margin-block:18px 6px">Storage and contact</h2>
    <p>Your browser stores a login token in browser storage; the native app uses local secure storage so you stay signed in across restarts, for up to 30 days. The native app can remember an optional device-unlock preference. Face ID, fingerprint and phone screen-lock authentication are handled by the operating system; the project does not receive biometric templates or your phone password. Sign out on shared devices. Pending transaction requests may be stored to prevent duplicate submissions. Camera frames and uploaded QR images are decoded on your device and are not uploaded to the server. Recovery emails use the configured email provider. Contact the project maintainer at vaibhavsh0120@gmail.com for questions or account deletion requests.</p>
  </main>
  <script>import '../lib/platform';</script>
</body>
</html>
